---
source: crates/core/tests/explain_text.rs
expression: text
---
HIT POLICY first: selected no rule
[ ] named (not fired): name STARTS WITH "Z"
    - name STARTS WITH "Z" is false (name = "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa...")
[ ] listed (not fired): labels IS NULL
    - labels IS NULL is false (labels = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, ...])
[ ] mapped (not fired): profile IS NULL
    - profile IS NULL is false (profile = {"a": [1, [...]], "b": "x\ny"})
[ ] typed (not fired): day = DATE "2026-01-01" OR rate = 0.5e0 OR price = 1.50 OR ok = FALSE
    would fire if any of these changed:
    - day = DATE "2026-01-01" is false (day = DATE "2026-02-03")
    - rate = 0.5e0 is false (rate = 0.25e0)
    - price = 1.50 is false (price = 1.25)
    - ok = FALSE is false (ok = TRUE)
[ ] "odd name" (not fired): `first name` = "Ana"
    - `first name` = "Ana" is false (`first name` = "Eva")
